# HydroTwin Project Rules & Hard Constraints

## 1. Honesty & Attribution
- ALL data is simulated and calibrated against published literature and reports.
- Every UI screen MUST display the prominent banner:
  `"Simulated data - not SONEDE or operator data"`
- An expandable "Assumptions" panel MUST be present on screens, documenting electricity tariffs, minimum pressures, outage windows, leak severity thresholds, and demand models.
- Never present simulated results as real savings.
- Tunisian water loss rates MUST always be quoted as a realistic range (25% to 50%), never a single misleading number.

## 2. Decision Support, Not Autonomous Control
- "The system ADVISES, humans DECIDE."
- Under no circumstances should the system trigger automated pump actuation or remote valve control.
- All recommendations must clearly provide actionable advice and a rationale for human water operators.

## 3. Decision Assistant & Offline Reliability
- The AI assistant rephrases structured outputs from the hydraulic and ML modules.
- It must NEVER hallucinate or invent a leak that has not been confirmed by the analytical pipeline.
- It must function 100% offline using deterministic template-based generation (with an optional LLM rephraser enabled strictly via environment variable).

## 4. Reproducibility & Fixed Seeds
- All stochastic processes (data generation, model training, sensor noise) MUST use fixed random seeds defined in `config.py`.
- Generated datasets and trained models must be persistable to `data/` and `models/`.
- The entire pipeline can be reproduced using standard scripts or `make`.

## 5. Honest Evaluation on Unseen Scenarios
- Evaluation MUST be conducted on unseen scenarios (different leak nodes, pipes, sizes, and demand conditions).
- Split by scenario, NEVER by row.
- Report honest metrics for both Rich (dense) and Sparse sensor configurations, documenting the performance drop.

## 6. Official Library API Adherence
- Never invent or fabricate library functions or APIs.
- Adhere strictly to WNTR and EPANET documented APIs and installed source code.

## 7. Fast Demo Speed & Precomputation
- Scenarios must respond within seconds.
- All heavy simulations and models must be precomputed and cached in `data/` and `models/`.
- A guided 6-step "Demo Mode" must load cached results for a seamless 3-minute live presentation.
